  "title": "fix: degraded review emits misleading zero-findings risk score",
  "description": "From sutra/104 review. When `build_findings` fails, `ReviewFindings::default()` (empty) is used and `compute()` produces a risk score as if there are zero violations. The `findings_degraded` flag is set but doesn't affect the risk_score field itself.\\n\\nFix: when findings_degraded is true, either omit risk_score or set it to null.\\n\\nFile: src/tools/review.rs:151-155,173",
